Where the knowledge comes from
------------------------------

The Remote Play protocol has no public specification. What is known about it
was worked out by the authors of two free-software projects, and this project
learns from their published work:

  Chiaki      Florian Märkl and contributors
              https://git.sr.ht/~thestr4ng3r/chiaki
  chiaki-ng   (first released as chiaki4deck) Street Pea and contributors
              https://github.com/chiaki-ng/chiaki-ng

Both are licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3, with
an exception for linking OpenSSL.

How they are used here:

  - The source code in this repository is written by the PS VulkanPlay authors.
    No source file of Chiaki or chiaki-ng is included in it.
  - Their source is read to learn how the protocol behaves. What is learned is
    written down under docs/protocol/ and implemented from there.
  - The differential tests (tools/oracle/) download chiaki-ng at a fixed commit
    into a scratch folder and compile parts of it into a test program, to check
    that our code gives the same results. That program is a test tool: it is
    not installed, packaged or distributed.
  - Fixed values that every client must send to be understood by a console are,
    by necessity, the same values in every implementation.


